        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cli): reject unknown models in config set",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users setting an unknown text-model reference with `openclaw config set` would see a successful config write, but the next agent run would fail later with `Unknown model`.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nChanged default and per-agent text-model primaries and fallbacks are now checked with the same prepared catalog and runtime model resolver used during inference before the config is persisted. Bare fallbacks are also rechecked when a default-primary provider change affects their meaning. Dry-run reports model failures in its structured validation result, including accurate checked/total completeness when resolver setup fails.\n\nMedia-model keys and unrelated config paths remain outside this validation. Valid configured-provider and catalog-backed model references keep their existing behavior.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUnknown model references are rejected immediately with the unresolved ref and a hint to run `openclaw models list`; the active config remains unchanged. Valid model references continue to set successfully, turning a confusing deferred runtime failure into an actionable set-time error.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Before the fix, an isolated config accepted `nonexistent-provider/nonexistent-model`, `config validate` reported valid, and a local agent run failed with `Unknown model: nonexistent-provider/nonexistent-model`.\n- After the fix, the same set command exits 1 with the unresolved ref and `openclaw models list` hint. The config SHA-256 remained `ca3d163bab055381827226140568f3bef7eaac187cebd76878e0b63e9e442356` before and after rejection.\n- A valid `openai/gpt-5.4-mini` set still exits 0 and is persisted.\n- Focused tests: 154 passed across `src/cli/config-model-validation.test.ts` and `src/cli/config-cli.test.ts`.\n- Targeted `oxfmt`, type-aware `oxlint`, and `git diff --check` passed.\n- `pnpm tsgo` passed on Blacksmith Testbox: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29706895331\n- Fresh branch autoreview reported no accepted or actionable findings.\n",
